{# ============================================================================
   THE ROSTER'S OVERVIEW TAB — the design's modules/roster/index.html, ported
   as far as it can honestly go today.

   WHAT IS HERE: the header, the six-tab strip (drawn by the shell from
   RosterModuleTabs), the Configure action, and the identity band.

   WHAT IS NOT, AND WHY IT IS NOT A PLACEHOLDER: the shipped composition under
   the band is `kpis · decisions · stations · map`, and every one of those four
   is a reading of PRESENCE — who checked in, whose claim the device disagrees
   with, which posts are reporting, where the pings put people. Presence is
   ruled to be the AREA's, read through a seam that has not landed. Drawing any
   of it today would mean inventing the one thing this module is ruled never to
   invent, so the band is where the page honestly stops.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ area.name }} · Roster{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Roster{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    {%- set stations = roster_url(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\AreaBundle\\Controller\\StationsController::ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) -%}
    Who is due, who checked in, and where their handset says they actually are. The stations and the live positions are the
    {%- if stations %} <a href="{{ stations }}">area&rsquo;s</a>{% else %} area&rsquo;s{% endif %}.
{% endblock %}

{% block roster_page %}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiRoster/_identity_band.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}
